  "query_preview": "..\nA few light rain showers or sprinkles are meandering around\nSEAZ this morning with flurries or a light rain/snow shower in \nthe mtns. This will continue through the morning with the best \nchance for sprinkles north of Tucson by afternoon. \n\nSunday into Monday will feature a drying and warming trend to \nnear average by Monday afternoon. The next shortwave will pass \nthrough the region late Monday night into early Wednesday with \nmore showers. Does not look like a very wet system right now, \nwith the best chance for showers north of the area. Gusty winds \nare also likely Tuesday afternoon as the system passes through. \n\nAnother dry period until a possible return to more unsettled \nweather next weekend. Daytime highs for the lower deserts \ngenerally in the upper 60s to lower 70s Sun-Tue with 60s the \nrest of the week.",
